The existing program already serializes each helper call with `join`. Calling `helper` directly avoids unnecessary thread creation, so there are no interleavings or thread-creation failures to account for.

```rust
fn helper() {}

fn call_sequence() {
    helper();
}

fn main() {
    call_sequence();
    call_sequence();
    println!("DONE done=1");
}
```
